[wistron][es1227] align LLDP CoPP CIR with Marvell policer quantum

The Marvell Prestera packet policer programs rates in 125-PPS quanta.
A CIR of 100 is truncated to zero, so queue4_group3 stops forwarding
LLDP, DHCP, and UDLD packets after its initial CBS is exhausted.

Raise CIR to the minimum non-zero hardware rate only for the Wistron
ES1227 36TS-P and 54TS-P2 platforms. Keep common SONiC defaults intact
for every other platform.

Apply with ./apply_patches.sh; do not commit this change directly into
the common source file.

diff --git a/files/image_config/copp/copp_cfg.j2 b/files/image_config/copp/copp_cfg.j2
index 520ae8a35..23355afe4
--- a/files/image_config/copp/copp_cfg.j2
+++ b/files/image_config/copp/copp_cfg.j2
@@ -37,6 +37,10 @@
 {% if DEVICE_METADATA is defined and DEVICE_METADATA['localhost'] is defined and DEVICE_METADATA['localhost']['type'] is defined and 'Mgmt' in DEVICE_METADATA['localhost']['type'] %}
 		    "cir":"300",
 		    "cbs":"300",
+{% elif DEVICE_METADATA is defined and DEVICE_METADATA['localhost'] is defined and DEVICE_METADATA['localhost']['platform'] is defined and DEVICE_METADATA['localhost']['platform'] in ['arm64-wistron_es1227_36ts_p-r0', 'arm64-wistron_es1227_54ts_p2-r0'] %}
+{# Marvell packet policers use 125-PPS rate quanta; CIR=100 is rounded down to zero. #}
+		    "cir":"125",
+		    "cbs":"100",
 {% else %}
 		    "cir":"100",
 		    "cbs":"100",
